# SOUND + LEAK-FREE — the `.enumerate()` SIBLING of
# `sound_for_string_elem_selfappend_plain.gg`.
#
# `lower_for_enumerate` carried its own copy of the String drop carve-out
# ("String borrows: don't register for drops"), so the class had exactly two
# write sites and Core #11 wants one fixture per sibling. This is the only
# fixture in the set that can see the enumerate drop registration: reverting
# that hunk alone leaves EVERY other row green.
#
# ⚠ THE INSTRUMENT IS `security_safe_no_leak` (`detect_leaks=1`), for the same
# reason as the plain sibling — the failure mode is a leak, and a
# `detect_leaks=0` run cannot see it.
#
# PINS the `.enumerate()` drop registration. RED-verified against the pre-fix
# compiler: rc 134 double free; and under a revert of that registration alone:
# `LeakSanitizer: 8 byte(s) leaked in 2 allocation(s)`, rc 99.
void main():
    Vector[String] v = Vector[String]()
    v.push("aa")
    v.push("bb")
    for i, s in v.enumerate():
        s = s + "!"
    for s in v:
        print(s)
